// V4: rules that make it feel part of the workspace
const rules4 = [["It has no window of its own", "No chat app, no floating bubble. Vane appears in the top bar, the panel, beside records and in drafts."], ["It uses the workspace's components", "Its cards, plans, flags and drafts are built from the same kit as every module: the same buttons, tables, shortcuts and focus ring."], ["It takes the workspace's theme", "Tender's orange in a retail workspace, Campus's in a school. Only the mark stays ink, so Vane is recognisable everywhere."], ["It speaks like a colleague", "First person, plain, with names and exact amounts. It ends with \"Let's …\". The button says the act: Send 3 reminders, never Do it."], ["It shows its working", "Every item can show the records it read and the SQL it ran. Nothing it says is unchecked."], ["It waits for a person", "Sending, paying, approving and changing are always a person's press, enforced on the server."], ["It respects people's time", "Quiet hours hold messages. Muted items stop coming back. One morning message, not a stream."], ["It is never called AI", "The interface says Vane. Claude is named once, on the Vane page in Management, as what Vane runs on."]];
